  "label": "User projected onto the squirrel as an existential-confused human",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual entity 'squirrel' through the anthropomorphic mapping established by the text 'i have no idea what i'm doing with my life'. The meme invites the viewer to identify with the squirrel's contemplative posture as a metaphor for their own existential confusion, creating a self-deprecating, relatable experience. This projection is implicit, using the squirrel as a stand-in for 'me' or 'you' in the context of internet meme culture.",
